  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics recorded $474M in contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics had 200,287 awards so far this fiscal year, and the average award size is $2.4K. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics obligations are down 37.1% year over year. Yearly obligations show a peak in FY25 at $753M, then fell to $474M in FY26. Past fiscal-year totals include $549M in FY21, $585M in FY22, $714M in FY23, and $704M in FY24. The FY2026 to date portfolio concentrates on a few large NAICS markets, led by Other Warehousing and Storage at $166M and Petroleum Lubricating Oil and Grease Manufacturing at $109M. The remainder of the top markets include Adhesive Manufacturing at $54.8M, Electrical Apparatus and Equipment and related wholesaling at $47.5M, and several smaller manufacturing and storage categories. These figures are contract obligations unless otherwise noted as total contract values in award tables.",
