        "heading": "How have obligations changed over recent fiscal years?",
        "body": "Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics obligations rose from $549M in FY21 to $753M in FY25, then declined to $474M in FY26. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics obligations are down 37.1% year over year. The trend shows growth through FY25 followed by a drop in the current fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What are Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics top markets in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics largest market is Other Warehousing and Storage at $166M. Asrc Federal Facilities Logistics also serves Petroleum Lubricating Oil and Grease Manufacturing at $109M, Adhesive Manufacturing at $54.8M, and Electrical Apparatus and Equipment, Wiring Supplies, and Related Equipment Merchant Wholesalers at $47.5M. Other top NAICS markets include All Other Miscellaneous General Purpose Machinery Manufacturing at $30.7M and Paint and Coating Manufacturing at $19.7M."
      }
